        "original_id": "6e7dafd9-3484-57c2-ad45-43c27d9be637",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Joy Formidable, Sixpence None the Richer\n- People: Leigh Nash\n- Music releases: A Heavy Abacus, Wishing for This, The Big Roar\n- Places: North Wales, London, New Braunfels, Nashville\n\nFacts:\n- The Joy Formidable is a Welsh alternative rock band that formed in 2007 in North Wales and is currently based in London, England.\n- Sixpence None the Richer is an American alternative Christian rock band that formed in New Braunfels, Texas, and later settled in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- \"A Heavy Abacus\" was released in July 2011 as the fifth and final single from The Joy Formidable's debut album \"The Big Roar.\"\n- Wishing for This is a Christmas EP by Leigh Nash, who is a member of Sixpence None the Richer.",
